| T A      | Ambient temperature for the suffix 6 version       | Maximum power dissipation | Maximum power dissipation | -40   |    85 | °C     |
| T A      | Ambient temperature for the suffix 6 version       | Low-power dissipation (5) | Low-power dissipation (5) | -40   |   105 | °C     |
| T A      | Ambient temperature for the suffix 7 version       | Maximum power dissipation | Maximum power dissipation | -40   |   105 | °C     |
| T A      | Ambient temperature for the suffix 7 version       | Low-power dissipation (5) | Low-power dissipation (5) | -40   |   125 | °C     |
| T A      | Ambient temperature for the suffix 3 version       | Maximum power dissipation | Maximum power dissipation | -40   |   125 | °C     |
| T A      | Ambient temperature for the suffix 3 version       | Low-power dissipation (5) | Low-power dissipation (5) | -40   |   130 | °C     |
| T J      | Junction temperature range                         | Suffix 6 version          | Suffix 6 version          | -40   |   105 | °C     |
| T J      | Junction temperature range                         | Suffix 7 version          | Suffix 7 version          | -40   |   125 | °C     |
| T J      | Junction temperature range                         | Suffix 3 version          | Suffix 3 version          | -40   |   130 | °C     |

1. When RESET is released functionality is guaranteed down to V BOR0  Min.
2. This formula has to be applied only on the power supplies related to the IO structure described by the pin definition table. Maximum I/O input voltage is the smallest value between Min(V DD , V DDA , V DDIO2 , V DDUSB , V LCD )+3.6 V and 5.5V.
3. For operation with voltage higher than Min (V DD , V DDA , V DDIO2 , V DDUSB , V LCD ) +0.3 V, the internal Pull-up and Pull-Down resistors must be disabled.
4. If T A  is lower, higher P D  values are allowed as long as T J does not exceed T Jmax  (see Section 7.10: Thermal characteristics ).
5. In low-power dissipation state, T A can be extended to this range as long as T J  does not exceed T Jmax  (see Section 7.10: Thermal characteristics ).

