## Output driving current

The GPIOs (general purpose input/outputs) can sink or source up to ±8 mA, and sink or source up to ± 20 mA (with a relaxed V OL /V OH ).

GPIOs PC13, PC14 and PC15 are supplied through the power switch, limiting source capability up to 3 mA only.

In the user application, the number of I/O pins which can drive current must be limited to respect the absolute maximum rating specified in Section 6.2 :

- The sum of the currents sourced by all the I/Os on V DDIOx,  plus the maximum consumption of the MCU sourced on V DD,  cannot exceed the absolute maximum rating Σ I VDD  (see Table 20: Voltage characteristics ).
- The sum of the currents sunk by all the I/Os on V SS , plus the maximum consumption of the MCU sunk on V SS , cannot exceed the absolute maximum rating Σ I VSS  (see Table 20: Voltage characteristics ).

