## 6.3.15 NRST pin characteristics

The NRST pin input driver uses the CMOS technology. It is connected to a permanent pullup resistor, R PU .

Unless otherwise specified, the parameters given in the table below are derived from tests performed under the ambient temperature and supply voltage conditions summarized in Table 23: General operating conditions .

Table 73. NRST pin characteristics (1)

| Symbol      | Parameter                               | Conditions            | Min           | Typ   | Max           | Unit   |
|-------------|-----------------------------------------|-----------------------|---------------|-------|---------------|--------|
| V IL(NRST)  | NRST input low level voltage            | -                     | -             | -     | 0.3 ₓ V DDIOx | V      |
| V IH(NRST)  | NRST input high level voltage           | -                     | 0.7 ₓ V DDIOx | -     | -             | V      |
| V hys(NRST) | NRST Schmitt trigger voltage hysteresis | -                     | -             | 200   | -             | mV     |
| R PU        | Weak pull-up equivalent resistor (2)    | V IN = V SS           | 25            | 40    | 55            | k Ω    |
| V F(NRST)   | NRST input filtered pulse               | -                     | -             | -     | 70            | ns     |
| V NF(NRST)  | NRST input not filtered pulse           | 1.71 V ≤ V DD ≤ 3.6 V | 350           | -     | -             | ns     |

